WEBVTT

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:11.150
Aren't I the odd one out?

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:13.110
Everyone else is male...

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:14.160
Now, now.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:16.380
It was fate that we ran into 
each other at the station.

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:18.480
Please stick around a little longer.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:21.350
Thanks to you, my first day 
off in a while is ruined.

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:24.760
You're this close to workplace harassment.

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:26.160
Kazari-kun...

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:27.510
What?

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:31.360
I'm really excited right now. Like a little boy.

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:34.410
That makes it closer to sexual harassment.

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:36.770
It's starting.

00:00:50.650 --> 00:01:11.800
Morgan! Drew! Morgan! Drew!

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:57.450
What are those?

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.800
Look, Kazari-kun!

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:15.310
Drew and Morgan.

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:19.470
They are Japan's world-class giant robots!

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:20.610
Huh?

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:30.610
<i>In response to an increase in heinous crimes,</i>

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:35.070
<i>a new movement is picking up steam in police 
and security forces around the world.</i>

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:40.920
<i>This is the story of the services 
performed by ACTIVE in Japan.</i>

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:54.770
<b>File 6: Dreams Beyond the Twilight</b>

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:58.020
I see...

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:01.740
<b>Special Exhibit 
Robots of Legend 
Howls of Steel</b>

00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:01.740
And here I was hoping you'd become a fellow fan.

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:05.300
When you're from a different generation, 
different things have nostalgic value.

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:07.240
Nostalgic value?

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:10.910
Japan used to be at the 
bleeding edge of robotics,

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:15.550
and their expertise with giant robots, 
in particular, was unparalleled.

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:20.180
You could say Drew and Morgan symbolize that.

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:22.060
Actually,

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:27.340
many years ago, I once rode on Drew's palm.

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:29.080
You did?

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:30.660
Aren't you jealous?

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:34.900
But why was it necessary for them 
to appear out of the water?

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:37.030
Because that's how it was

00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:39.340
traditionally done in anime.

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:40.800
Huh? Anime?

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:44.540
Back in the day, there were lots 
of anime series with robots.

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:47.560
Kids who loved that stuff grew up

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:51.480
and worked to make their dreams 
of developing robots come true.

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:54.500
Their dreams fueled an entire genre's growth.

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:56.540
Is that seriously true?

00:03:56.850 --> 00:03:58.980
Growing up, my dream was

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:01.630
to become a robot pilot.

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:03.300
Huh...

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:08.370
These are the scientists and small factory 
artisans who devoted their lives

00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:10.470
to giant-robot development.

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:11.850
Small factories?

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:13.570
Without their superior technique

00:04:13.570 --> 00:04:16.030
and passion for their work,

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:21.450
Drew and Morgan would have 
never seen the light of day.

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:24.540
This was a while ago,

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:26.650
but I once rode on Drew's palm—

00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:28.550
You already told me that.

00:04:28.550 --> 00:04:29.330
Ah.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:32.850
<b>Twilight Technology</b>

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:32.310
But in the end, giant robots were...

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:33.050
Yes.

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:35.990
Though it was hoped they'd be 
optimal for dangerous work,

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:39.870
such as construction or excavation, 
or for disaster relief,

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:43.070
fuel inefficiency was their weakness.

00:04:43.070 --> 00:04:45.260
And the damning strike was...

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:46.520
Willwears.

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:49.330
Right. With greater functionality 
and cost effectiveness,

00:04:49.330 --> 00:04:53.050
the Willwears' emergence 
sealed the robots' fate.

00:04:53.050 --> 00:04:56.730
Development of giant humanoid 
robots went rapidly into decline.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:05:00.570
The final blow was the 
Third Quicksand Phenomenon.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:05:03.900
<b>The Third Quicksand Phenomenon</b>

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:02.790
The Kanto Bottomless Belt, right?

00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:03.570
Yes.

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:06.310
The area with a high 
small-factory concentration

00:05:06.310 --> 00:05:08.320
is now an evacuation zone.

00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:10.660
Can they still move?

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:12.120
Morgan can.

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:16.120
But they couldn't figure out 
what was wrong with Drew.

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:17.990
The technology's too old.

00:05:17.990 --> 00:05:18.540
Hey!

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:19.820
Back away from the railing!

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:20.790
It's not safe.

00:05:21.350 --> 00:05:22.080
Hey!

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:23.090
Jeez...

00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:24.010
It's that geezer again.

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:26.370
The rivets are crying.

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:28.800
The rivets are crying...

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:28.800
Are you okay? Are you hurt?

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:30.270
We've told you many times.

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:31.560
The rivets are crying...

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:31.560
What's the matter?

00:05:32.050 --> 00:05:35.300
Oh, he's from a nearby hospice.

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:36.620
Hospice?

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:38.760
This isn't his first time here.

00:05:38.760 --> 00:05:40.600
We keep warning him, but...

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:42.640
Well, he's quite advanced in years.

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:44.860
Let's go, Grandpa.

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:45.840
Wait a minute.

00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:49.200
Are you, by chance, Dr. Kasumigaseki?

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:53.920
You know who this is?

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:57.920
I'm certain that he's the father 
of Drew and Morgan...

00:05:57.920 --> 00:05:58.580
Huh?

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:01.980
Dr. Kasumigaseki!

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:06.550
<b>Nursing Home 
Light of Musashi</b>

00:06:09.450 --> 00:06:12.850
On good days, he can recall a lot.

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:15.230
That's when he's absolutely amazing!

00:06:15.230 --> 00:06:18.640
He'll take apart broken TVs and 
vacuum cleaners in a flash,

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:20.650
and fix them like magic!

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:22.040
Does he have any family?

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:24.120
No, he doesn't seem to.

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:27.000
But I think he has a visitor sometimes,

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:29.100
one of his old colleagues.

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:31.330
Yes, that would be me.

00:06:31.630 --> 00:06:35.620
I'm the only one who lives nearby now.

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:38.630
I thought Dr. Kasumigaseki was still tasked

00:06:38.630 --> 00:06:41.850
with Drew and Morgan's maintenance,

00:06:41.850 --> 00:06:45.710
even after robot development was canceled.

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:46.960
It was the government.

00:06:47.980 --> 00:06:51.730
When the area around his factory became 
a designated evacuation zone,

00:06:51.730 --> 00:06:55.050
the government confiscated the robots.

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:59.810
I heard it was some moneymaking 
scheme by the officials.

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:03.440
Where did the artisans involved 
in robot development go?

00:07:04.530 --> 00:07:06.890
They switched to careers in industries

00:07:06.890 --> 00:07:10.400
where they could still apply their skills, 
like rail transport and aeronautics.

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:12.220
Just like I did.

00:07:12.670 --> 00:07:15.380
These clocks are becoming bygone artifacts,

00:07:15.380 --> 00:07:17.580
but I do get repair requests once in a while.

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:19.100
I see.

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:20.390
We...

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:25.060
We were all putting our hearts and 
souls into careers we believed in.

00:07:25.060 --> 00:07:28.780
We never thought we'd see 
a whole field disappear.

00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:32.840
Now I wonder what our dreams even were...

00:07:38.250 --> 00:07:40.550
I'm sorry to have kept you so long.

00:07:40.850 --> 00:07:43.190
You can go now, Kazari-kun.

00:07:43.190 --> 00:07:44.630
What about you, Funasaka-san?

00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:47.980
I'll ask around to see if Dr. Kasumigaseki 
can maintain those robots again.

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:49.470
There's nothing to lose.

00:07:49.470 --> 00:07:51.450
You really want to go that far?

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:55.600
He is a great scientist and a national treasure.

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:57.620
That isn't the only reason, though.

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:07.450
Back then, I was sneaking into the factory

00:08:07.450 --> 00:08:10.360
almost every night because I wanted to see Drew.

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:11.340
But...

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:16.760
I-It moved!

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:19.830
You're trespassing. I'm calling the police.

00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:24.440
You're the one who's been sneaking into 
the factory every night, aren't you?

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:27.280
Well, yeah. The security here sucks.

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:28.660
Lemme go, mister.

00:08:28.660 --> 00:08:29.980
Don't call me "mister."

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:31.310
I'm a doctor.

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:32.820
Dr. Kasumigaseki.

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:35.040
I love robots!

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:37.700
Just once in my life, I'd love to pilot one!

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:41.170
Hmph. Then you should seriously 
pursue becoming a pilot.

00:08:41.170 --> 00:08:42.170
A pilot?

00:08:42.170 --> 00:08:43.210
That's right.

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:47.390
You should try to become Drew's pilot.

00:08:47.390 --> 00:08:49.410
And don't slack off.

00:08:49.410 --> 00:08:51.430
Study hard and work toward your dreams!

00:08:51.430 --> 00:08:53.090
Study?

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:55.890
If that doesn't appeal to you, I'll report trespass—

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:56.170
Um, wait!

00:08:56.170 --> 00:08:57.700
Not that, please!

00:08:57.700 --> 00:08:59.140
So will you do it or not?

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:01.000
Me, a pilot?

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:03.730
Okay, that doesn't sound bad.

00:09:05.470 --> 00:09:06.790
All right, doc.

00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:08.960
I'll become Drew's pilot.

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:10.650
I promise!

00:09:11.620 --> 00:09:13.610
I'll be waiting for you, boy.

00:09:13.610 --> 00:09:14.500
Okay!

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:18.710
To him, it might have been a trivial lecture.

00:09:19.010 --> 00:09:21.270
But having a dream to work toward

00:09:21.270 --> 00:09:23.790
is a big deal for boys.

00:09:24.340 --> 00:09:26.210
I'm only here today

00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:30.470
because he gave me a dream that day.

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:33.340
I couldn't fulfill my promise from back then,

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:35.080
but I'd like to repay him, at least.

00:09:35.510 --> 00:09:36.630
Is that strange?

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:47.180
Damn this robot exhibit.

00:09:47.180 --> 00:09:49.610
They took Morgan from me.

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:56.150
Logos?

00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:58.890
They're the ones who sent 
me a weird e-mail before.

00:10:03.370 --> 00:10:05.920
Hey! What the hell?!

00:10:06.220 --> 00:10:08.020
It's on autopilot?

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:10.940
Wh-What the...

00:10:13.990 --> 00:10:15.170
What's this?

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:19.580
No way... It was true?

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:24.370
<i>We open at 10 AM.</i>

00:10:24.450 --> 00:10:27.390
<i>We open at 10 AM.</i>

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:28.520
<i>We open at—</i>

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:46.040
<b>The fuel tank is full. 
There's an overseas escape route. 
Come on Morgan.</b>

00:10:47.880 --> 00:10:51.380
Logos is more hardworking than I thought.

00:10:53.730 --> 00:10:55.840
Sorry to keep you waiting, Morgan.

00:10:55.520 --> 00:10:56.210
<b>Mo
(Fury)</b>

00:10:56.210 --> 00:10:58.230
Let's launch!

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:02.680
What?

00:11:02.680 --> 00:11:05.360
We're up against a giant
humanoid heavy machine?

00:11:05.360 --> 00:11:06.950
This has to be a joke.

00:11:06.950 --> 00:11:08.800
It's at least twenty meters tall.

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:10.600
Are you sure it's still working?

00:11:10.990 --> 00:11:12.290
Funasaka-san...

00:11:13.340 --> 00:11:16.320
Morgan was stolen?

00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:25.810
The stolen giant humanoid heavy machine

00:11:25.820 --> 00:11:29.790
is moving from Okachimachi to Akihabara 
along the Yamanote Break Water.

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:33.550
It's not responding to any contact.

00:11:33.950 --> 00:11:36.670
Kazari-kun, do we have any security 
camera footage from the area?

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:38.050
Putting on main screen.

00:11:42.470 --> 00:11:43.720
It's Morgan!

00:11:44.020 --> 00:11:46.440
It's about to pass by the Third Anime Center.

00:11:46.740 --> 00:11:48.970
Local authorities seem to have 
placed a cordon, but...

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:56.110
Stop! Stop! Are you listening to us?

00:12:09.420 --> 00:12:11.710
As soon as we arrive at Akihabara's 
special use platform,

00:12:11.710 --> 00:12:14.810
Kuroki-kun and Sena-kun are 
to suit up, understood?

00:12:14.810 --> 00:12:15.730
Roger.

00:12:15.730 --> 00:12:17.140
You can count on us!

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:18.460
Boss...

00:12:20.070 --> 00:12:21.300
I have a request.

00:12:26.180 --> 00:12:28.190
Vitals, all green.

00:12:28.520 --> 00:12:29.010
Lock.

00:12:34.350 --> 00:12:36.860
Inner unit, begin output.

00:12:36.860 --> 00:12:40.340
Oscar II, set strike interceptor unit.

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:55.270
Understood. You are free to act as you wish.

00:12:55.590 --> 00:12:57.460
Asami-chan, please provide backup support.

00:12:57.460 --> 00:12:58.250
Huh?

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:02.920
Okay, going ahead.

00:13:09.210 --> 00:13:09.860
Heh.

00:13:10.180 --> 00:13:12.370
So what if it's a giant humanoid machine?

00:13:12.370 --> 00:13:15.670
It's just an antique with nothing but sheer size.

00:13:15.670 --> 00:13:17.020
It's no match for us.

00:13:17.570 --> 00:13:19.420
Though I hate to admit it, I agree.

00:13:19.420 --> 00:13:21.640
But its sheer mass is a problem.

00:13:21.640 --> 00:13:24.150
Let's deal with it before there's 
any more collateral damage.

00:13:24.150 --> 00:13:25.080
Got it!

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:27.820
This is the police. Power down the 
humanoid machine immediately.

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:30.380
There you are, Willwear.

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:32.240
Pests!

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:43.210
Wh-Why am I so sleepy?

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:48.430
Oscar II!

00:13:48.430 --> 00:13:50.930
Oscar I, cut external monitors,

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:52.750
and put some distance between 
you and the machine!

00:13:52.750 --> 00:13:53.180
What?

00:13:53.180 --> 00:13:56.170
The humanoid machine has 
a sleep-induction device

00:13:56.170 --> 00:13:58.460
developed by Nemuron.

00:13:58.460 --> 00:13:59.900
A sleep-induction device?

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:03.190
It works by using vibrations 
at a specific wavelength

00:14:03.190 --> 00:14:04.920
to deliver sleep-inducers to the brain.

00:14:04.920 --> 00:14:07.150
It's limiter's been removed. It's very dangerous.

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:09.370
Wake up, Oscar II!

00:14:09.770 --> 00:14:10.880
Oscar II!

00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:14.310
Even asleep, you lack class!

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:22.420
The vibration's effective range
is approximately fifty meters.

00:14:24.620 --> 00:14:26.550
Then I'll just maintain range and attack.

00:14:28.820 --> 00:14:31.260
I think that'd be a bad idea.

00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:32.140
What?

00:14:32.140 --> 00:14:33.190
Why?

00:14:33.190 --> 00:14:36.400
That machine's heavily armored to the extreme.

00:14:36.400 --> 00:14:38.980
With no data on it, it's impossible 
to deduce good targets.

00:14:38.980 --> 00:14:41.810
A mistake could lead to collateral damage 
to the city from ricochets.

00:14:44.880 --> 00:14:47.220
Using civilians as hostages...

00:14:47.520 --> 00:14:50.030
Funasaka-san, Madoka-chan found 
what you requested.

00:14:50.030 --> 00:14:53.450
This is the suspect. 
We're pretty sure he's the perp.

00:14:54.110 --> 00:14:56.120
Shimura Makoto, age fifty-two.

00:14:56.120 --> 00:14:59.020
He received official pilot training back then.

00:14:59.020 --> 00:15:02.640
He was supposed to be Morgan's pilot.

00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:05.920
Morgan's official pilot...

00:15:06.570 --> 00:15:08.910
But the project was canceled,

00:15:06.710 --> 00:15:18.520
<b>Name: Shimura Makoto 
Place of Birth: Bunkyou Ward, Tokyo Prefecture 
Profession: Unemployed 

00:15:08.910 --> 00:15:11.630
and his life thereafter is the 
picture of a downward spiral.

00:15:11.980 --> 00:15:15.930
He's also suspected of sending 
numerous harassing e-mails

00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:18.430
intended to prevent the robot exhibit.

00:15:19.890 --> 00:15:21.020
What's this?

00:15:21.340 --> 00:15:22.650
Shimura's apartment.

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:24.690
I had local authorities stream their feed.

00:15:31.640 --> 00:15:33.700
An unforgotten dream, huh?

00:15:35.350 --> 00:15:39.460
Boss, can you get permission 
to launch Drew, stat?

00:15:39.460 --> 00:15:40.710
Okay, got it.

00:15:41.530 --> 00:15:43.060
Why Drew?

00:15:43.060 --> 00:15:46.560
Because only Drew can stop Morgan now.

00:15:46.560 --> 00:15:48.890
But Drew's broken.

00:15:48.890 --> 00:15:50.550
Even if it could start up,

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:53.090
once it gets close to Morgan, 
the sleep-induction will...

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:54.840
That won't happen.

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:56.430
If I were him,

00:15:56.690 --> 00:15:59.320
I wouldn't turn down a 
chance at a robot battle.

00:15:59.750 --> 00:16:00.680
Ever!

00:16:00.680 --> 00:16:02.100
You're sure confident!

00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:06.940
Please, doctor...

00:16:07.410 --> 00:16:09.120
The Morgan you created

00:16:09.420 --> 00:16:13.010
is being used for evil by 
a thoughtless individual!

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:16.210
Only Drew can save us from this crisis.

00:16:16.210 --> 00:16:17.350
You can do this...

00:16:17.350 --> 00:16:19.620
No, only you can do this,

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:21.330
Dr. Kasumigaseki!

00:16:25.100 --> 00:16:26.260
Please!

00:16:26.610 --> 00:16:27.750
Doc!

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:29.670
You're the one from the clock shop.

00:16:29.670 --> 00:16:31.810
I've gathered the old crew.

00:16:31.810 --> 00:16:33.880
We'll help, doc!

00:16:33.880 --> 00:16:35.260
Let's do this, doc!

00:16:36.760 --> 00:16:39.760
Let's bring Drew back to life!

00:16:40.980 --> 00:16:43.560
Thank you all for your help!

00:16:44.850 --> 00:16:46.170
My lab coat.

00:16:49.960 --> 00:16:52.570
My lab coat! Hurry up!

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:54.350
Dr. Kasumigaseki!

00:16:54.350 --> 00:16:55.640
Doc!

00:16:56.030 --> 00:16:58.500
First, remove the rusted rivets.

00:16:58.500 --> 00:16:59.170
Yes, sir!

00:16:59.490 --> 00:17:01.720
I have a pretty good idea what the issue is.

00:17:01.720 --> 00:17:04.680
It's just one part. Don't dawdle! Hurry!

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:07.540
Oscar II to command vehicle.

00:17:07.540 --> 00:17:08.460
Good morning.

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:12.840
Oscar II, your priority is to minimize damage.

00:17:12.840 --> 00:17:15.180
Lure the target to the mud zone as best you can.

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:15.870
Roger!

00:17:15.870 --> 00:17:16.720
We'll do our best.

00:17:17.060 --> 00:17:18.090
Carry it!

00:17:18.090 --> 00:17:19.680
Hurry up and link it up!

00:17:25.140 --> 00:17:26.340
Funasaka-san?

00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:30.020
By the way, who's going to pilot Drew?

00:17:30.020 --> 00:17:32.360
I will, of course.

00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:33.870
You?

00:17:34.190 --> 00:17:37.260
When I was a boy, I wanted to be a pilot.

00:17:37.260 --> 00:17:39.930
I still remember how to pilot it as clear as day.

00:17:40.270 --> 00:17:41.740
It was just an online course, though.

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:43.450
An online course?

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:46.370
I'm counting on you, young Funasaka!

00:17:46.680 --> 00:17:47.380
Yes,

00:17:47.380 --> 00:17:48.420
doc!

00:17:53.270 --> 00:17:54.170
It activated.

00:17:55.790 --> 00:17:56.730
Good.

00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:08.650
Drew,

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:10.060
launch!

00:18:34.250 --> 00:18:37.250
Now that I've wreaked havoc, 
I have no regrets.

00:18:37.250 --> 00:18:40.030
All I have to do now is reach the 
location Logos designated and escape.

00:18:40.030 --> 00:18:41.680
Stop right there, Morgan!

00:18:45.520 --> 00:18:46.910
Hey, that voice...

00:18:46.910 --> 00:18:47.980
Funasaka-san?

00:18:47.980 --> 00:18:50.310
I won't let you have your way any longer!

00:18:50.310 --> 00:18:52.900
Drew! Great idea!

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:17.510
Command vehicle, sending live footage.

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:20.600
Funasaka-san, are you okay?

00:19:20.600 --> 00:19:23.840
Command vehicle, we think we 
can apprehend the perp now.

00:19:23.840 --> 00:19:25.770
Let Funasaka-san handle it.

00:19:25.770 --> 00:19:27.160
Don't make any rash moves.

00:19:27.600 --> 00:19:31.020
I will not let anyone use robots for evil!

00:19:31.600 --> 00:19:33.900
Drew Drill Punch!

00:19:34.290 --> 00:19:35.940
Get off your high horse!

00:19:37.030 --> 00:19:38.530
Morgan Shovel!

00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:39.530
Funasaka-san!

00:19:42.500 --> 00:19:45.060
Morgan is more powerful!

00:19:45.060 --> 00:19:48.560
Admit defeat before this power!

00:19:49.150 --> 00:19:50.390
Full action, huh?

00:19:58.940 --> 00:20:00.670
This isn't good. If we don't do something...

00:20:01.290 --> 00:20:05.050
Take this steel-clad metal fist!

00:20:06.650 --> 00:20:08.020
And now...

00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:12.560
Funasaka-san!

00:20:12.780 --> 00:20:15.250
Funasaka-san, don't lose!

00:20:16.980 --> 00:20:18.620
Goodbye, Drew.

00:20:29.910 --> 00:20:32.810
The world's best robot pilot

00:20:33.370 --> 00:20:34.580
is me.

00:20:38.420 --> 00:20:40.920
Run, Funasaka-san!

00:20:46.230 --> 00:20:48.110
What's wrong, Morgan?

00:20:48.110 --> 00:20:49.330
Why won't you move?

00:20:49.330 --> 00:20:50.310
Why?!

00:20:51.890 --> 00:20:53.070
It's out of fuel?

00:20:53.380 --> 00:20:54.730
Bingo!

00:20:58.890 --> 00:21:00.190
Perp apprehended.

00:21:02.390 --> 00:21:03.700
Funasaka-san...

00:21:04.940 --> 00:21:07.270
You'll only last so long at full action.

00:21:07.780 --> 00:21:09.870
You should have known

00:21:10.170 --> 00:21:11.890
that this fuel inefficiency

00:21:11.890 --> 00:21:14.750
drove the giant robots into ruin.

00:21:18.250 --> 00:21:20.760
<i>Yesterday evening, in an unprecedented case,</i>

00:21:20.760 --> 00:21:24.760
<i>a giant humanoid heavy machine on display 
at the robot exhibit was stolen,</i>

00:21:22.210 --> 00:21:28.430
<b>Former Pilot Involved 
Giant Humanoid Heavy Machine Stolen from Robot Exhibit</b>

00:21:24.760 --> 00:21:26.930
<i>and another humanoid heavy machine</i>

00:21:26.930 --> 00:21:29.170
<i>was deployed to bring it under control.</i>

00:21:29.470 --> 00:21:32.810
<i>Shimura Makoto, age fifty-two and 
unemployed, was arrested...</i>

00:21:30.470 --> 00:21:34.390
<b>Nursing Home 
Light of Musashi</b>

00:21:32.810 --> 00:21:35.150
I'm sure the doctor will be thrilled

00:21:35.150 --> 00:21:37.350
to learn he can work with robots again.

00:21:37.740 --> 00:21:40.170
What strings did you have to pull?

00:21:40.170 --> 00:21:41.840
That's a trade secret.

00:21:41.840 --> 00:21:44.490
Our success in this case helped, as well.

00:21:45.040 --> 00:21:47.260
Oh... Thank you for your help yesterday.

00:21:47.560 --> 00:21:50.450
Can we see Dr. Kasumigaseki?

00:21:50.450 --> 00:21:52.450
Well...

00:21:55.950 --> 00:21:57.720
It happened early this morning.

00:21:57.720 --> 00:21:58.920
Oh, no...

00:21:59.560 --> 00:22:01.880
But look at his face.

00:22:01.880 --> 00:22:03.960
He looks so happy.

00:22:05.970 --> 00:22:07.050
Doctor...

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:51.910
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:50.930 --> 00:23:52.260
Ohakonyapachininko!

00:23:51.950 --> 00:24:04.920
File 7: Long Rail Life

00:23:52.260 --> 00:23:55.830
Thanks to all the Haruka-san 
fans for your patience!

00:23:55.830 --> 00:23:58.380
As far as I can tell, she'll play 
a big role next week!

00:23:58.380 --> 00:24:00.130
I think, probably...

00:24:00.130 --> 00:24:01.520
Sorry if I'm wrong.

00:24:01.520 --> 00:24:02.670
"Long Rail Life."

00:24:02.670 --> 00:24:04.950
Let's watch together again next time!
